<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Nixcon on João Thallis</title><link>https://joaothallis.com/tags/nixcon/</link><description>Recent content in Nixcon on João Thallis</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 06 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://joaothallis.com/tags/nixcon/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Continuously Integrating Your Nix Config</title><link>https://joaothallis.com/posts/continuously-integrating-your-nix-config/</link><pubDate>Sat, 06 Sep 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://joaothallis.com/posts/continuously-integrating-your-nix-config/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NixCon 2025&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;September 6, 2025, from 16:00 to 17:00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OST, Rapperswil-Jona, Switzerland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Presented with Claudio Neto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="about-the-workshop" class="relative group"&gt;About the workshop &lt;span class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700" style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#about-the-workshop" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This hands-on workshop showed how to add continuous integration checks to Nix configurations. Participants built automated pipelines to test and build configurations, lint code, and catch configuration errors on each change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://talks.nixcon.org/nixcon-2025/talk/B9S93H/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Official NixCon session page&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://github.com/joaothallis/continuously-integrating-your-nix-config" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Slides&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Infecting Your Server with NixOS</title><link>https://joaothallis.com/posts/infecting-your-server-with-nixos-at-nixcon-2024/</link><pubDate>Sat, 26 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://joaothallis.com/posts/infecting-your-server-with-nixos-at-nixcon-2024/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NixCon 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;October 26, 2024, at 14:35&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;bUm, Berlin, Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="about-the-workshop" class="relative group"&gt;About the workshop &lt;span class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700" style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#about-the-workshop" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Installing NixOS on a server can be challenging for beginners or time-consuming when installing it on multiple machines. This workshop explored how to make the process simpler and which tools can help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I wrote a 
 
 &lt;a href="https://joaothallis.com/posts/infecting-your-server-with-nixos/"&gt;step-by-step guide to installing NixOS with nixos-infect&lt;/a&gt; to help prepare for and follow along with the workshop.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Monitoring Your System Using NixOS</title><link>https://joaothallis.com/posts/monitoring-your-system-using-nixos/</link><pubDate>Sat, 26 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://joaothallis.com/posts/monitoring-your-system-using-nixos/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NixCon 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;October 26, 2024, at 18:00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;bUm, Berlin, Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="about-the-talk" class="relative group"&gt;About the talk &lt;span class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700" style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#about-the-talk" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This talk explores using NixOS to configure and manage monitoring for applications and NixOS systems with Prometheus and Grafana.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://talks.nixcon.org/nixcon-2024/talk/RY98HT/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Official NixCon session page&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8WOwedX9X5E" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;YouTube recording&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Introduction to nix-bitcoin</title><link>https://joaothallis.com/posts/introduction-to-nix-bitcoin-at-nixcon-2024/</link><pubDate>Fri, 25 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://joaothallis.com/posts/introduction-to-nix-bitcoin-at-nixcon-2024/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NixCon 2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;October 25, 2024, at 16:45&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;bUm, Berlin, Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="about-the-talk" class="relative group"&gt;About the talk &lt;span class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700" style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#about-the-talk" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This talk explores nix-bitcoin, a project that uses NixOS to simplify the secure deployment and management of Bitcoin nodes. It also demonstrates deploying NixOS systems with krops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://talks.nixcon.org/nixcon-2024/talk/XPXBHT/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Official NixCon session page&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ld8GNQNRO90" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;YouTube recording&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>